@page "/sales/debit-notes"
@inherits PageBase

@*
    Why this thin page exists — do NOT fold this route back into `SaCdnList.razor`:

    The sales credit-note and debit-note lists are the SAME screen, but they must be served by two
    DIFFERENT page types. Neither URL carries a route parameter, so when the menu navigates client-side
    from /sales/credit-notes to /sales/debit-notes the router resolves the same component type and
    REUSES the existing instance — `OnInitialized` never runs again, so the title, the hero, the
    per-family menu rights, the e-Invoice toolbar and the grid stayed on the family the operator arrived
    on, and only a full page load (which builds a new instance) corrected it.

    With two page types the router disposes the old page and creates the new one, so the screen is
    always rebuilt for the URL that is actually showing. `SaCdnList` itself resolves the family from the
    URL (`ResolveFamily()`), so it renders correctly when hosted here.

    The same pattern is used for the purchase pair (`PoCdnDebitList`) and the self-billed pair
    (`PoSbCdnDebitList`).
*@

